{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"565e90a9-9c6c-43d8-8ecc-141b1ba65d96","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have identified the cause of the cache eviction issue and fixed it.\n\n### Root Cause\nPreviously in [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-KWzCjd/bot.py#L130-L136), [`build_system()`](file:///tmp/h-KWzCjd/bot.py#L130-L136) concatenated the static coaching instructions (`INSTRUCTIONS`) and the per-athlete context (`athlete_context(a, today)`) into a single text block marked with `cache_control`. Because Anthropic's prompt caching relies on exact prefix matching, every call to `save_fact` appended a new entry to `athlete.facts`, altering the text in that single block. This caused the prompt cache to miss on subsequent calls (`cache_read_input_tokens: 0`, `cache_creation_input_tokens: ~1000+`), forcing the API to pay full price for the entire system prompt.\n\n### Solution\nIn [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-KWzCjd/bot.py#L130-L136):\n- Split the system prompt into two blocks:\n  1. **Static Block:** Contains `INSTRUCTIONS` with `{\"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}`. Because this block remains identical across requests, athletes, and `save_fact` updates, it stays cached.\n  2. **Dynamic Block:** Contains `athlete_context(a, today)` without `cache_control`, allowing facts and dates to change dynamically without invalidating the cached instructions prefix.\n\nDetails of the diagnosis and changes have been written to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-KWzCjd/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":154.263973,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":160302,"output_tokens":4088,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":891176,"total_tokens":164390}}}
